HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_A_Details", "(A) Emitter State is set to Self, causing per-emitter loop control. Switch to System if unnecessary."),
HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_B_Details", "(B) No CutoutTexture is assigned to translucent Sprite Renderers. When particles overlap, using CutoutTexture to deform polygons can reduce overdraw and improve performance."),
HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_C_Details", "(C) When only one particle exists, changing Source Mode to Emitter skips particle array generation and update processing to reduce rendering cost."),
HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_D_Details", "(D) Renderer count in the NiagaraSystem exceeds {0}, which may raise GPU and memory cost."),
HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_E_Details", "(E) Mesh Renderers sample SkeletalMeshes, which increases rendering cost in Niagara."),
HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_F_Details", "(F) Mesh Renderers use meshes with DistanceField enabled, which can increase Niagara rendering cost."),
HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_G_Details", "(G) Mesh Renderers use meshes with collision. Niagara mesh particles do not use StaticMesh collision, so it can be removed."),
HC4UE_ENTRY_LOCTEXT("Niagara_Emitter_Optimization_Hints_H_Details", "(H) Mesh Renderers use meshes with multiple UV channels. Effect meshes rarely need multiple UVs; remove unused channels."),
